Z||000009||Cheever2||06-15-2001||01:17 AM||||I don't believe it.  This is <B>exactly</B> what Galen & I were discussing in the chat earlier this evening - how I would paint my Fino (when I get it <I>someday</I>).<P>Here's my brilliant suggestion:<BR>Paint it like a road.  <P>Understand?  If not, then park it on the street and look at it straight-on from the front.  Paint the base color like the road you usually drive (generally there are two: blacktop and concrete).  Continue the yellow line and white line in the places on the car that match the places on the road.  Do the same from the rear, and try to match the image from the front somewhere in the middle.<P>This would be the automotive version of camouflage!  Imagine evading the speed traps... the cops won't see you coming or going.  You might get more pedestrians stepping out in front of you, but what are the witnesses going to say - "Honest, officer, the road just came up and <I>grabbed</I> the old lady!"<P>When I get time I'll attempt to edit a photo and post an example.<P>(Is this your latest contest, Arch?  Did I win?  What do I get?)<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000010||Oreif||06-15-2001||01:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>British Racing Green or Forest Green Metallic. Tan interior Fieros look awesome with those type of deep metallic greens..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with Haze, A Metallic British Racing Green would be GREAT on that car! Even before I read the later posts I was thinking the B.R.G.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||14
