Z||000013||CoolBlue87GT||06-15-2001||03:25 AM||||Okay, here are my idea's -- now don't freak, these pic are not a Fiero, just posting for the paint design only.  I created this on my 1979 Mercury Capri.<P>This might give you an idea, maybe not, but hope you enjoy it.<P>We used Black, charcoal, silver,red, and<BR>clear paint, and lots of tiny 1/16" pin stripes between the colors. (hard to see)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Capri_e.jpg">  <BR>The main Red stripe is painted, and goes around the car, down the sides, and the roof, and is connected all around.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Capri_~3.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Capri_h.jpg"> <BR>The finish was sharp like a mirror .<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Capri_d_1.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000014||Phil||06-15-2001||06:39 AM||||Just paint it Clear and be done with it.||||reg||1
Z||000015||FieroLT1||06-15-2001||07:35 AM||||Alright! Here are my choices Archie... in order or preference:<P>1. Midnight Blue Metalic (BMW 540i)<BR>2. Blackhawk Night Pearl (Honda Accord)<BR>3. Midnight Pine Pearl (Lexus SC450)<P>Gotta like the darker colors  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>To get a better feel for these you can check out. BMW.com, Honda.com and Lexus.com and select configurator or build your own.<P>Good luck. I am sure any color you pick will look awesome.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
