Z||000020||Pontiaddict||06-15-2001||08:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>Here's my brilliant suggestion:<BR>Paint it like a road.  <P>Understand?  If not, then park it on the street and look at it straight-on from the front.  Paint the base color like the road you usually drive (generally there are two: blacktop and concrete).  Continue the yellow line and white line in the places on the car that match the places on the road.  Do the same from the rear, and try to match the image from the front somewhere in the middle.<P>This would be the automotive version of camouflage!  Imagine evading the speed traps... the cops won't see you coming or going.  You might get more pedestrians stepping out in front of you, but what are the witnesses going to say - "Honest, officer, the road just came up and <I>grabbed</I> the old lady!" </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm sorry, but what are you going to do when there's a big freakin truck heading right for you that doesn't know you're there. The owners of silver cars should know what I'm talking about. It's bad enough that most people in cars can't see you already because your car is only 4 foot tall. Don't make it harder on yourself. Then again, I've always liked the dark grey primered street rods.<P>As for the Fino, I suggest Limefire Green. For those who don't know, it's a semitransparant green with alot of gold pearl.<BR>||||reg||1
